WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.827 --> 00:00:03.577
(clapping hands)

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.530
- [Interviewer] Flat Top,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.890
tell me where you grew up.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.590
- Um, I was born in
Starkville, Mississippi.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.292
I grew up a young country man.

00:00:17.292 --> 00:00:19.459
(mumbles)

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.823
At two, three years old,

00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:27.260
I hunted, I fished, I did climbing

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.550
climbing the trees and riding the horses,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.780
the whole nine yards.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.793
I'm talking about from, from,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.310
running through berry bushes to

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:43.870
picking out of the garden.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:44.850
You know, I didn't chop the

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.080
lot of rows since I was young, man,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.141
and I'd been through a whole lot

00:00:49.141 --> 00:00:52.240
in the years that I grew up, man.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.490
Especially coming from the country,

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.323
from the country to the city?

00:00:54.323 --> 00:00:55.839
- [Interviewer] When'd you come out to LA?

00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:58.341
- I came out to LA in '79.

00:00:58.341 --> 00:00:59.810
- '79.
- '79.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.670
- [Interviewer] So you were how old then?

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.370
- I was nineteen years old.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.203
- [Interviewer] Nineteen.

00:01:04.203 --> 00:01:06.282
And you got involved with gangs

00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:07.115
at what point?

00:01:07.115 --> 00:01:08.459
- At nineteen years old.

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:09.454
- [Interviewer] Right then?

00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:13.479
- Right then. South Central. Yes indeed.

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:14.890
- [Interviewer] Which gang?

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.320
- I'm from Harlam Crip.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.320
Yes, sir, (mumbles).

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.043
Stayed over that for 39 years.

00:01:22.911 --> 00:01:23.744
My first,

00:01:25.643 --> 00:01:26.550
my attempted murder,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.410
was at 19 years old.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.833
- [Interviewer] Oh, so you...
- I was just six months.

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:31.666
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:35.060
- Six months and they gave me a gun to

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.613
go try to gun somebody down.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.433
And I think I was as
scared as the guy was.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.750
At 19 years old, sir,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.830
you're not thinking about going

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:46.663
to kill nobody.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.497
But, during that time,

00:01:50.497 --> 00:01:52.933
either you did them or they did you.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.291
Your home is your home gang,

00:01:55.291 --> 00:01:56.360
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.350
It was like, it was like turning

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.520
your back on them.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.433
But, you know,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.300
I did what I did

00:02:06.586 --> 00:02:09.980
and, at 19 and 20 years old

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.483
I did another attempt.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.873
But you know, the fighting,

00:02:16.824 --> 00:02:19.242
and the stabbing and the cutting,

00:02:19.242 --> 00:02:21.713
all these scars that I've got on my body,

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.747
before I was 21 years
old I got shot twice.

00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:26.771
- [Interviewer] So you didn't get

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:28.700
thrown in jail? Or prison?

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.390
- No, I didn't close.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.255
Never got caught.

00:02:31.255 --> 00:02:32.088
- [Interviewer] Never got caught?

00:02:32.088 --> 00:02:33.066
- Never got caught.
- [Interviewer] Now let me

00:02:33.066 --> 00:02:34.233
back up a bit.

00:02:36.581 --> 00:02:38.750
Was it this change of environment

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.360
that kind of got you into
this violent lifestyle,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.550
or did you have some childhood...

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.004
- No, it was change of environment.

00:02:44.004 --> 00:02:44.837
- [Interviewer] It was
change of environment.

00:02:44.837 --> 00:02:47.220
Did you grow up with both
parents or one parent?

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.053
- Both parents.

00:02:48.053 --> 00:02:48.886
- [Interviewer] Both parents.

00:02:48.886 --> 00:02:50.344
Normal childhood...
- Normal childhood.

00:02:50.344 --> 00:02:51.177
- [Interviewer] Country boy growing up

00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:52.810
in Mississippi...
- Country boy going to

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.790
church every Sunday.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:55.623
- [Interviewer] And then you

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:56.707
come out to this...
- Come out to here and...

00:02:56.707 --> 00:02:57.540
- [Interviewer] Get yourself involved in

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.768
violence and peer pressure to be violent.

00:02:59.768 --> 00:03:01.930
- To be violent.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.740
And it turned me into that person.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.130
That I didn't really want to be,

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.052
but because I had joined this gang,

00:03:08.052 --> 00:03:11.037
that's what it was, so...

00:03:11.037 --> 00:03:12.290
- [Interviewer] And in that neighborhood,

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.454
there's no other option other than

00:03:13.454 --> 00:03:15.222
join a gang?
- No other option.

00:03:15.222 --> 00:03:16.850
- [Interviewer] You couldn't become

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:20.740
an A student and become...
- That wasn't gonna happen.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.203
I think out of my hood,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.610
in the 30 years I'd been there,

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.794
I maybe know two head students

00:03:26.794 --> 00:03:29.280
that actually went to college.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.113
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:30.113 --> 00:03:35.002
Because, everything else was street life.

00:03:35.002 --> 00:03:37.067
You know, you was raised in the streets.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.410
And I was raised in the streets.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.258
- [Interviewer] So back to your,

00:03:40.258 --> 00:03:41.793
your 21 years old?

00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:43.693
- 21 years old.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.823
Man, I went on a drive by.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.040
And, it was women and kids.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.300
To where they're pointing,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.883
my homeboys didn't care.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.070
But I did.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.660
Because I could not kill no

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:05.723
women or no kids.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.380
Because them young people
had did none to me.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.804
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:10.804 --> 00:04:13.650
And I got disciplined for that.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.360
- [Interviewer] For kind of standing up?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.415
- For not shooting up,

00:04:16.415 --> 00:04:17.840
- [Interviewer] For not shooting them?

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.003
- I got really disciplined.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:21.770
To the point where I was in the

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.523
hospital for five days.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:28.400
Yes, they are, they are treacherous.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.781
When it comes to,

00:04:29.781 --> 00:04:34.781
to upholding your place in a gang.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.000
Especially if you're in one of

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.450
the ones I come from.

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:43.450
You know, and 22, 23 years old,

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.720
I was in Pelican Bay.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.803
Pelican Bay for assault
with a deadly weapon.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.740
It was an iron pipe to one of

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.433
my enemies heads from,
from, from twenties.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.210
But, the thing about it,

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:05.043
he didn't die.

00:05:05.043 --> 00:05:06.743
But, you know, he came close.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.390
And, being that I was so young,

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.793
my first time in prison,

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.100
it scared me to death.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.400
Because Pelican Bay was the

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.943
worst prison in California.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.143
And at the age of 24 years old,

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.910
man, it was like you was being

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:28.863
reborn all again.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.820
Because you was told when to eat,

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.560
when to shit, when to move,

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.210
when to sleep.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.973
And, I wasn't used to that.

00:05:38.754 --> 00:05:43.513
So, about nine months into Pelican Bay,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.950
I caught another shoot term.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.880
Thirteen more shoots.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.593
They sent me from Pelican Bay to Corcoran.

00:05:51.771 --> 00:05:54.030
Corcoran, therefore you only come out

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.923
of your cell for one hour a day.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.680
So I did these thirteen months

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.650
for one day out of a week

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.230
and you picked the day.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.920
Your showers came to your cell,

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.490
your food came to your cell,

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.440
your mail came to your cell,

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.740
everything came to your cell.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.490
And when we used to go outside

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.780
it was a lot of tension between

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.920
the blacks and the essays.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.220
Why?

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.591
Because of the COs.

00:06:23.591 --> 00:06:25.759
They used to bet on that.

00:06:25.759 --> 00:06:26.592
- [Interviewer] What?

00:06:26.592 --> 00:06:29.320
- The COs, the correction officers,

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.070
used to bet who would win these

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.803
fights between the
blacks and the Mexicans.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.120
Until one person got killed

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.082
and they found out about it and

00:06:39.082 --> 00:06:41.600
it blew up in their face.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.400
Because they would, say me for instance,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.217
they would put me in a cage

00:06:46.217 --> 00:06:50.453
and five minutes later
here come five essays.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:52.513
Into the same cage.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.323
Now what's the first, my first, reaction?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:58.940
Let's get closer to the door and

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.160
hit the first one come in,

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.530
cause there was no other alternative.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.540
- [Interviewer] Essays are...
- Hispanics.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.700
Yeah, gang members, and

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.750
back then you had some gang members that,

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.596
Hispanics that would kill a black

00:07:12.596 --> 00:07:16.850
before they would eat a piece of bread.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.303
Believe me, and, so,

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.770
when I got out of Corcoran,

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.060
out of Corcoran's (mumbles),

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.887
I came home.

00:07:25.887 --> 00:07:28.690
Back downtown, homeless.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.223
At the age of 24 years old.

00:07:32.137 --> 00:07:34.103
Out here on these streets,

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.760
people manipulate you.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.513
They, they try to take over your mind.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.610
They try to take over
anything that you got.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.820
But me being raised the way I was raised,

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.290
I'm a very strong person

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.730
to the point of where I see through

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.410
a whole lot of the bull crap that

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.563
they was bringing.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.610
And two years down here, sir,

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:01.793
I got shot right here.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.530
I was dancing, I was
dancing on the sidewalk,

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.201
me and three girls.

00:08:08.201 --> 00:08:11.193
And the same dude that
I hit with this pipe,

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:14.613
is the one that shot me.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.340
He tried to shoot me in my back.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.760
I know that's what he
was really trying to do

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.733
to paralyze me.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.930
'Cause, uh, I heard through the

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:24.590
grapevine that he didn't want me to die,

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.483
he just wanted me to be paralyzed.

00:08:27.679 --> 00:08:29.340
So I could roll around in that shell

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.140
the rest of my life.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.430
But because of one of the

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.900
ladies standing behind me

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.163
told me he had a gun, I turned.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.880
And therefore it hit me here,

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.483
instead of in the spine.

00:08:42.483 --> 00:08:44.512
'Cause it was a .45,

00:08:44.512 --> 00:08:47.173
it would have really, really torn me up.

00:08:47.173 --> 00:08:49.639
(siren wail)

00:08:49.639 --> 00:08:51.630
After that, after that gun shot, man,

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.193
I got into smoking crack cocaine.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.700
Very, very, very, very heavy.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.990
I'm talking about at least a half ounce

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.720
to an ounce a day.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.630
- [Interviewer] How much is that?

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.460
- That's maybe, three to four hundred

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:08.633
dollars a day.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.670
And, I'm to like this...

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.520
I would be up for seven, eight,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.600
nine, ten days at a time.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.730
Drinking and smoking and running around.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.990
I would go a hundred miles in a

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:25.540
five block radius.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.690
Five block radius and I would go

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:31.310
through them five blocks
in them days, man,

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.849
a hundred miles in a day.

00:09:32.849 --> 00:09:34.253
Just back and forth.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.443
On that crack BS.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.400
Crack led me to going to prison again.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.250
I went back to prison for a burglary.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.543
A residential burglary.

00:09:46.494 --> 00:09:48.244
And this was in 1992.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.510
I ended up back in Corcoran.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:53.343
Beyond.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.380
Six months into Corcoran,

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.139
we had a riot.

00:09:59.139 --> 00:10:00.793
Blacks against the Mexicans.

00:10:02.361 --> 00:10:05.170
It was, it was 29 people

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.420
that had to be air lifted

00:10:07.276 --> 00:10:10.480
from Corcoran shoot to the hospital.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.220
Because, there was a lot of stabbing.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.790
You know, when you in prison back then

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.750
in them times, man,

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:21.330
it wasn't all fighting
and you know that's it,

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.433
it was a lot of people getting stabbed.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.660
And, thank god I wasn't one of them.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:29.713
But you know,

00:10:32.038 --> 00:10:33.450
I get out again.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.603
I get out of prison.

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.460
Back downtown.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:38.327
Back downtown.

00:10:38.327 --> 00:10:40.470
Ohhh, I'm gonna go into a program,

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.300
I'm gonna do that right thing.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.263
Go to a program, say maybe,

00:10:45.594 --> 00:10:48.400
estimate eight days.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.210
I'm back on the street.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.540
Back with the same routine.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.024
Same people.

00:10:54.024 --> 00:10:55.429
That's why I say,

00:10:55.429 --> 00:10:57.680
if you do the same thing over and over,

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.010
you're gonna get the same results.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.900
So, I'd been trying, every now and then,

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.760
try and live a little bit different.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:05.867
But, like I tell people,

00:11:05.867 --> 00:11:10.110
if I'm not ready, can't
nobody make me ready

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.320
to stop using drugs.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.740
I've been using drugs
since I was 13 years old.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.022
- [Interviewer] Do you
still use them today?

00:11:16.022 --> 00:11:17.580
- I still use drugs to this day

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.063
and I'm 59 years old.

00:11:20.248 --> 00:11:23.070
And I know I don't look it,

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.990
because penitentiary
preserves you, believe me.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:30.573
I really did 25 years
of my life in prison.

00:11:30.573 --> 00:11:32.323
And I've been to 13 penitentiaries.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:35.703
And that's bad to say.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.423
But, it is what it is
when you're a gang banger.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.733
Gang banging led me to a life of misery.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:50.250
And, '96...

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:54.233
'96, I was terrible.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.520
I didn't care about nothing.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.403
Or nobody.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:03.843
I was smoking crack and shine, together.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:09.050
Which was a deadly mixer.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:10.193
I mean deadly.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.970
To where, the crack
put me in a happy mood.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:16.303
The shine put me in a bad mood.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:20.310
And, I had the shine
take over the good mood,

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:21.320
now I'm in a bad mood.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.207
Now I want to fight everybody,

00:12:23.207 --> 00:12:25.786
